Subject: [PATCH 07/11] d3d10umd: negotiate the WDDM 2.0 D3D11 DDI and report typed UAV loads

The Yttrium KMD reports WDDM 2.0, and the D3D11 runtime then asks the UMD
for the WDDM 2.0 DDI. The UMD now supplies the changed view, rasterizer,
query, flush, relocation, hardware-protection and resource-layout entry
points and the DXGI 1.4 table. It reports a 32-bit GPU VA range per resource
(zero made CreateDevice fail with 887a0020) and advertises additional typed
UAV loads only after checking host storage-image support for every required
format. Maps R10G10B10A2_UINT for typed loads. Protected resources,
conservative rasterization and overlays stay unsupported.

Prior art: F11-F14 (R/NATIVE-WDDM20.md "Native D3D11").
Origin: codex working tree R/mesa (git diff 374c3022), re-exported by
vmlab-win3d build/mesa; see build/mesa/README.md.
